      "question": "Based on the FY2024 filings, compare the primary strategic objectives of AEP and ED.",
      "expected_answer": "AEP's filing does not explicitly state a strategic objective in the provided excerpts; it lists risk factors. ED's filing states: 'Con Edison seeks to provide shareholder value through continued dividend growth, supported by earnings growth in regulated utilities and electric transmission projects.' Thus, ED has a clear shareholder-focused strategy, while AEP's excerpt concentrates on forward-looking statements and risks.",
      "predicted_answer": "**Conclusion:** ED explicitly states a primary strategic objective focused on shareholder value through dividend growth supported by regulated utility earnings and transmission investments, while the supplied AEP Item 7 excerpts do not contain an explicitly stated primary strategic objective.\n\n- **AEP FY2024:** The retrieved Item 7 excerpts consist entirely of forward-looking statement disclaimers and risk factors (economic conditions, regulatory changes, fuel costs, capital availability, etc.). No explicit primary strategic objective is stated in the supplied evidence [E1][E3].\n\n- **ED FY2024:** The company explicitly states it \"seeks to provide shareholder value through continued dividend growth, supported by earnings growth in regulated utilities and electric transmission projects\" [E2].\n\n**Comparison:** ED frames its strategy around shareholder returns via regulated utility and transmission growth, whereas the scoped AEP Item 7 excerpts disclose risks without articulating a parallel strategic objective.\n\nSources:\n[E1] AEP_2024.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\n[E2] ED_2024.html — Item 7. The Companies' Strategies May Not Be Effective To Address Changes In The External Business Environment\n[E3] AEP_2024.html — Item 7. Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations",
